<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaPairos — Halachah 3<br>Part 1 (Introduction + §§ 1–6)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE · Based on <span class="lr">LM I:37</span></span></div>
<div class="lm">Topic of <i>Birchas HaPairos</i>. Based on the <i>Torah</i> <span class="v">"Dirshu Hashem V'Uzo"</span> (<span class="lr">Siman 37</span>) — see the entire <i>Torah</i> there.</div>

<div class="p"><b>Summary of the <span class="h">Torah</span>:</b> Body and soul are the aspects of <span class="h">adam</span> and <span class="h">behaima</span>, light and darkness, wisdom and folly, <span class="h">zikaron</span> [memory] and <span class="h">shich'chah</span> [forgetfulness] — the wisdom of Torah versus external wisdoms which are folly compared to Torah wisdom. One must subdue the material — the aspect of death, the folly of the body of the four elements, as stated in the Zohar — through fasting, etc. The reward of fasting is <span class="h">tzedakah</span>. There are two levels of <span class="h">tzedakah</span>: <span class="h">tzedakah</span> in <span class="h">chutz la'Aretz</span> and <span class="h">tzedakah</span> in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is greater. Similarly two levels of Torah — Torah from breath that has sin versus Torah from breath without sin: <span class="mx">"the world endures only through the breath of schoolchildren,"</span> etc. Through <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> [the air of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>] and breath without sin, the <span class="h">Avos</span> are revealed in the world to protect, <span class="h">din</span> and darkness are pushed away, the material and folly are subdued, and the intellect — the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, Torah, light, life, and <span class="h">chesed</span> — are elevated. <span class="mx">"One who fasts is called a chasid"</span> — <span class="v">"one who benefits his soul is a man of chesed"</span> — for he nullifies <span class="h">din</span> and darkness and draws <span class="h">chasadim</span>, which is <span class="h">gemilas chesed</span> to his <span class="h">nefesh</span>, i.e. to Torah.</div>

<div class="p">The root of Torah is the <span class="h">kavod</span> [honor] of Hashem: <span class="v">"for My honor I created it."</span> Therefore through the honor given to the elder who forgot his learning, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span> are elevated. <span class="v">"Be careful with the jugular veins"</span> — the blood is the <span class="h">nefesh</span> reincarnated for rectification; the <span class="h">shochait</span> must intend to elevate the <span class="h">nefesh</span> in the blood. The essential lack of <span class="h">parnassah</span> comes only through unfit <span class="h">shochtim</span>; the fit <span class="h">shochait</span> feeds Israel by elevating the souls to the <span class="h">Shechinah</span>. <span class="v">"Be careful with the children of the <span class="h">amai ha'aretz</span>, for from them Torah will go forth"</span> — they are precious souls caught like birds in a snare; through honoring them, Torah is revealed from concealment — for the root of Torah is <span class="h">kavod</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 1 — <i>Birchos HaNehenin</i> Elevate the <i>Nefesh</i> Through <i>Avira d'Eretz Yisrael</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of <span class="h">birchos hanehenin</span> — it is forbidden to enjoy this world without a <span class="h">berachah</span>. For it is known: through the <span class="h">berachah</span> one recites on a fruit or the like, one elevates the reincarnated <span class="h">nefesh</span> there. For in everything in the world there are reincarnated souls. Therefore the essential <span class="h">berachah</span> is in the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> — so that the food is included in <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> through the <span class="h">berachah</span>. For <span class="v">"there Hashem commanded the blessing — life"</span> — <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is the source of all <span class="h">berachos</span>. There all prayers, <span class="h">berachos</span>, and thanks ascend. All <span class="h">birchos hanehenin</span> are derived from <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>: <span class="mx">"if he blesses afterward, certainly beforehand."</span> The essence of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> is in the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless Hashem your G-d for the good land."</span></div>

<div class="p">All <span class="h">birchos hanehenin</span> are to elevate the <span class="h">nefesh</span> in what one eats. Therefore all <span class="h">birchos hanehenin</span> must be in the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> — <span class="v">"and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless... for the good land"</span> — from which we derive all <span class="h">berachos</span>. To elevate the <span class="h">nefesh</span> through <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is the breath of schoolchildren without sin. When one blesses on something, <span class="v">"the power of His works"</span> is revealed — one reveals through the <span class="h">berachah</span> that Hashem created the entire world. The essential holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is through <span class="v">"the power of His works"</span> — through revealing that Hashem created everything, as Rashi explains on <span class="v">"Beraishis,"</span> as Rabbainu writes in many places.</div>

<div class="p">It emerges: through the <span class="h">berachah</span> — revealing that Hashem created this thing — that thing is included in the holy air, <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>, whose essential holiness comes only through <span class="v">"the power of His works."</span> Wherever Israel are, revealing and publicizing holiness — revealing that Hashem created everything — <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness is drawn there, the aspect of <span class="h">mikdash me'at</span>. Through the <span class="h">berachah</span>, the thing is included in <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>, and through this the <span class="h">nefesh</span> reincarnated there is elevated. For the essential elevation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is through <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is why our Sages cautioned to treat foods with honor — not to disgrace them, as stated in <span class="h">Shulchan Aruch</span>. One must treat foods with honor so the <span class="h">nefesh</span> there is elevated through <span class="h">kavod</span>, which is the root of everything, as explained in the aforementioned <span class="h">ma'amar</span>. It emerges: the essential <span class="h">berachah</span> on everything is in the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> — the breath of schoolchildren. This is why the order of <span class="h">berachos</span> is taught to children at the beginning of their studies — the essential <span class="h">berachah</span> is through the breath of schoolchildren without sin, the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>. There is the source of blessing: <span class="v">"He will bless the youths."</span> Through this the <span class="h">Avos</span> are revealed to protect, <span class="h">din</span> and darkness are pushed away, the material and forgetfulness are subdued, and <span class="h">chesed</span>, wisdom, life, and <span class="h">zikaron</span> are drawn.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 2 — Keeping <i>Berachos</i> Makes One a <i>Chasid</i>; <i>Nezikin</i> and the <i>Nefesh</i></div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="mx">"whoever wants to be a chasid should fulfill the matters of Berachos."</span> Through the <span class="h">berachah</span> one elevates the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">chesed</span> is drawn — <span class="v">"one who benefits his nefesh is a man of chesed."</span> Through <span class="h">berachos</span>, one is a <span class="h">chasid</span>. <span class="mx">"And some say: the matters of Avos"</span> — the essential <span class="h">berachos</span> are in the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>, through which the <span class="h">Avos</span> are revealed: <span class="v">"and I will remember My covenant with Yaakov... and the land I will remember."</span> <span class="mx">"And some say: the matters of Nezikin"</span> — all laws of damages involve removing harm from another. Through this, <span class="h">din</span>, the aspect of damage, is pushed away.</div>

<div class="p">For money is the root of the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, as Rabbainu writes elsewhere (<span class="lr">Siman 59</span>). The <span class="h">ma'amar</span> also hints at this: through <span class="h">tzedakah</span> one elevates the <span class="h">nefesh</span> — for a poor man is considered as dead, lacking money to sustain his <span class="h">nefesh</span>, since holy money is the root of the <span class="h">nefesh</span>. When one gives <span class="h">tzedakah</span> to the poor, one revives and establishes his <span class="h">nefesh</span>: <span class="mx">"whoever sustains one soul of Israel..."</span> Through the money given to the poor, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and intellect are elevated: <span class="v">"fortunate is the one who is wise toward the poor"</span> — <span class="mx">"there is no poor but in da'as"</span> — for it is all one. Since he lacks money, which is the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and intellect, he is also poor in <span class="h">da'as</span>: <span class="v">"the wisdom of the poor is despised."</span> Through giving him money, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and intellect are elevated — and the giver's <span class="h">nefesh</span> is elevated too: <span class="mx">"whoever has compassion on creatures, they have compassion on him."</span></div>

<div class="p">This itself is the aspect of the laws of <span class="h">nezikin</span>: the Torah warns not to rob or damage another — so as not to blemish the <span class="h">nefesh</span> which is the aspect of money. If one robbed or damaged, one must return and pay — to complete the <span class="h">nefesh</span> through restitution. <span class="h">Nezikin</span> = elevation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> = <span class="h">tzedakah</span>. Therefore through this one is called a <span class="h">chasid</span>. Monetary cases require three judges — the three <span class="h">Avos</span>: <span class="mx">"there is no 'many' fewer than three, which are the Avos"</span> (Tikkunim). Through proper monetary judgments, <span class="h">din</span> is pushed away and the <span class="h">nefesh</span> whose root is in money is elevated — the <span class="h">Avos</span> are revealed. The judges' essential wisdom comes from <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> which gives wisdom: <span class="mx">"it is forbidden to judge except by those with semichah, and semichah is only in Eretz Yisrael"</span> — we function as emissaries of the earlier ones (<span class="h">Choshen Mishpat</span>). When there is judgment below, there is no judgment above — <span class="h">din</span> is pushed away, <span class="h">chesed</span> is drawn — all through <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 3 — Precedence in <i>Berachos</i>: <i>Kavod</i> Reveals the <i>Nefesh</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the laws of precedence in <span class="h">berachos</span>. The essential elevation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is through <span class="h">kavod</span>, the root of everything — through which the <span class="h">nefesh</span> desires to be included in its root. Therefore one must know which fruit to bless first — one must give honor to the fruit that has a greater <span class="h">nefesh</span>, and therefore must be given more honor by blessing it first. Through <span class="h">kavod</span>, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is revealed from concealment — <span class="v">"be careful with the children of amai ha'aretz, for from them Torah goes forth."</span> Therefore one must treat foods with honor. This is the aspect of a royal table — <span class="v">"the King of kavod"</span> — the essential <span class="h">kavod</span> is at eating.</div>

<div class="p">This is why specific <span class="h">berachos</span> have more importance and precedence than general ones — e.g. <span class="v">"borai pri ha'aitz"</span> and <span class="v">"borai pri ha'adamah"</span> precede <span class="v">"shehakol."</span> At first glance this is puzzling — a general <span class="h">berachah</span> should be more important since one praises Hashem for creating everything: <span class="v">"that everything came into being through His word."</span> But the advantage of a specific <span class="h">berachah</span> in precedence is: when one blesses a specific fruit with its own <span class="h">berachah</span>, it has a greater share of <span class="h">kavod</span> — one mentions Hashem's praise for this fruit alone, singling it out. This is because the souls there are more honored. Therefore one must honor them more and give them precedence — the essential elevation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is through <span class="h">kavod</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The essential importance for precedence is the fruits of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — whichever is earlier in the verse takes precedence, as our Sages said. For the essential <span class="h">berachah</span> is in the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Our Sages said: <span class="mx">"the entire verse was said for measures."</span> The greatness of the Seven Species with which <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is praised is that these fruits have very lofty souls — the essential importance of fruits. The <span class="h">nefesh</span> is Torah. Therefore the fruits of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — the Seven Species — are used to measure all the measures of Torah, indicating the lofty souls within them. Therefore they have precedence — one must honor them more because they contain more Torah and <span class="h">nefesh</span> than other fruits.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 4 — <i>Kazayis</i>: Olive = Body and Soul, Forgetfulness and Memory</div>

<div class="p">This is why all Torah measures are in a <span class="h">kazayis</span> [olive-size], and all eating measures are in a <span class="h">kazayis</span>, and <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> and the final <span class="h">berachah</span> require a <span class="h">kazayis</span>. For the olive with its oil indicates the aspect of body and soul, forgetfulness and memory. Olives cause forgetfulness, but the oil that comes from olives is the opposite — oil aids memory, as is brought. So olive and oil are the aspects of forgetfulness and memory — body and soul. The <span class="h">nefesh</span>, the aspect of memory, is Torah and <span class="h">da'as</span>. Therefore all Torah measures are in a <span class="h">kazayis</span> — Torah, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and memory, is in the aspect of the olive's oil. Just as oil cannot be revealed from the olive except through crushing — so too the Torah and <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span> can only be revealed through crushing and beating the body, breaking the material's folly and subduing forgetfulness. Then the light of the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, Torah, and <span class="h">zikaron</span> is revealed from within the body and forgetfulness. As our Sages said: <span class="mx">"Torah endures only in one who kills himself over it."</span> This is <span class="v">"pure olive oil, crushed for illumination"</span> — the Zohar: <span class="mx">"wood that does not catch fire is beaten; a body in which the soul's light does not rise..."</span> The olive with its oil = body and soul. Therefore all Torah measures are in a <span class="h">kazayis</span> — all Torah <span class="h">mitzvos</span> are specifically through body and soul. When the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is clothed in the body, then the essential Torah fulfillment — the essential revelation of Torah and <span class="h">nefesh</span> is from within the body, in the aspect of <span class="mx">"the advantage of light from darkness."</span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 5 — Eating a <i>Kazayis</i> Requires a Final <i>Berachah</i>: <i>Zikaron</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore the measure of eating is a <span class="h">kazayis</span>, and then one must recite a final <span class="h">berachah</span>. The essential eating is for the <span class="h">nefesh</span> — <span class="v">"a tzadik eats to satisfy his soul"</span> — so the <span class="h">nefesh</span> shines more through incorporating the souls within the food eaten in holiness and purity with proper <span class="h">berachah</span> and <span class="h">kavanah</span>. Therefore the eating measure is a <span class="h">kazayis</span> — the aspect of Torah, body and soul, forgetfulness and memory — for the essential eating is to elevate and illuminate the <span class="h">nefesh</span> from within the body.</div>

<div class="p">This is why the Torah warns especially about <span class="h">zikaron</span> at the time of eating: <span class="v">"lest you eat and be satisfied... and your heart grow haughty and you forget... and you shall remember Hashem your G-d, for He gives you strength."</span> At eating, one must be especially careful not to blemish the <span class="h">zikaron</span> — the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, Torah — not to follow the desiring body. Rather the opposite: subdue and nullify the body during eating — break the body's desires — eating in holiness in the aspect of <span class="v">"a tzadik eats to satisfy his soul"</span> — so that through eating, the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, <span class="h">zikaron</span>, and Torah are elevated more.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 6 — First <i>Berachah</i> Has No Measure; Final <i>Berachah</i> Requires <i>Kazayis</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore the final <span class="h">berachah</span> requires a measure — a <span class="h">kazayis</span> — but the first <span class="h">berachah</span> has no minimum measure. For <span class="h">zikaron</span> and <span class="h">shich'chah</span> only apply when one already has some <span class="h">da'as</span> — then one must guard the <span class="h">zikaron</span> not to forget the <span class="h">da'as</span> attained. This is the essential completeness of <span class="h">da'as</span> — from within the body, <span class="mx">"the advantage of light from darkness."</span> For <span class="h">da'as</span> at its root has no measure — Torah is His unity, which is <span class="h">Ein Sof</span>. But Hashem in His mercy contracted the Torah's light into letters and measures so we could receive it while clothed in the body. Through the Torah/<span class="h">da'as</span>/<span class="h">nefesh</span> being clothed in the body — the aspect of measures — there comes <span class="h">zikaron</span> and <span class="h">shich'chah</span>. The <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> grips essentially through contraction and measure — the body. But this is the essential completeness: attaining <span class="h">da'as</span>/<span class="h">nefesh</span>/<span class="h">zikaron</span> from within the body and forgetfulness.</div>

<div class="p">This is the first and final <span class="h">berachah</span>. The first has no measure — before eating, the <span class="h">nefesh</span>/<span class="h">da'as</span> has not yet been revealed at all; one must bless to begin revealing the <span class="h">da'as</span>. This has no measure — the initial revelation of <span class="h">da'as</span> is beyond measure. But the final <span class="h">berachah</span> is to guard the <span class="h">da'as</span> and <span class="h">nefesh</span> received and illuminated through eating — that one not come to <span class="h">shich'chah</span> but remain in <span class="h">zikaron</span>. Therefore the final <span class="h">berachah</span> requires a measure — as long as there is no measure, one has not yet come to <span class="h">shich'chah</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span>. <span class="h">Zikaron</span> only applies when one has <span class="h">da'as</span> received in measure. Then one must guard the <span class="h">zikaron</span> — the essential completeness of <span class="h">da'as</span>. The measure is a <span class="h">kazayis</span> — memory emerging from forgetfulness.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore the eating measure is a <span class="h">kazayis</span>. The essential eating — satisfaction — comes from the <span class="h">nefesh</span> clothed within, the <span class="h">chiyus</span> of the food. Before a <span class="h">kazayis</span>, it is not called eating at all. The essential <span class="h">nefesh</span> is only when in the aspect of olive-oil — <span class="h">da'as</span>/<span class="h">nefesh</span> drawn into measure, arriving at <span class="h">zikaron</span> and <span class="h">shich'chah</span> — the essential completeness of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">da'as</span>. Then when eating a <span class="h">kazayis</span>, the clothed <span class="h">nefesh</span> has the power to satisfy the person — when one eats in holiness, elevating the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span>, subduing the body and <span class="h">shich'chah</span>.</div>

